// ikma_controller_neptune.vdf
//
// Session 64 (2026-10-16) - the IKMA Steam Deck controller layout. Zamar,
// Session 63: "I would like to make us an official IA control template for
// use on the steamdeck with our controls."
//
// Built from Valve's "Gamepad With Joystick Trackpad" template
// (controller_base/templates/controller_neptune_gamepad_fps.vdf), the layout
// Zamar got IKMA's controls working with on his Deck. Every group below is
// that template, unchanged except the back grips: each Deck control sends
// the Xbox controller input in the same position, which is what IKMA's
// controller map reads.
//   - Face buttons, D-pad, bumpers, triggers, both sticks and stick clicks:
//     the matching Xbox controls. View = SELECT, Menu = START.
//   - Left trackpad: D-pad, on click. Right trackpad: right stick.
//   - Back grips (Session 64, Zamar: "Home L4, End L5, Control plus Space
//     R4, R5 empty for now."). Steam names the upper grips L4/R4
//     (button_back_left_upper / button_back_right_upper) and the lower ones
//     L5/R5 (button_back_left / button_back_right). The grips send keyboard
//     keys; IKMA keeps them on the pad (KeyIn.DeckGripKey).
// Name, Session 64, Zamar: rename it to "Inscryption Access Official".
// Description: Zamar's own wording, from the layout he published (Steam
// Workshop 3820918554, Session 64). The French line is still the old draft.
// export_type personal_local: how Steam marks a layout saved on this Deck
// (Steam lists it under Your Layouts; file <appid>/<name>_0.vdf).
"controller_mappings"
